    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9363" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commēto</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conm-</span></b> ), āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq. n.</i>
			[commeo, II.], <i>to go frequently</i>, Afran. and
			Novius ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 89, 30 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad mulierculam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 3, 1, 35</span></i>
			.—With acc. of distance: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nam meus scruposam victus conmetat viam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 1, 2, 82</span></i>
			.</div>
